"""pfwho — which pf.conf rule decided a described first packet, and what
translation was applied to it on the way.

Static adjudication over a pf.conf file (plus its include / load-anchor
tree and table files). Never invokes pfctl, never reads the live
ruleset or /dev/pf, never does DNS. Semantics pinned in
DESIGN-pfwho.md (PF01-PF38): OpenBSD 7.0 primary dialect, FreeBSD 14.0
as a second evaluation mode (separate translation phase, PF06).
Stdlib only.
"""
